it's hard to anticipate what might  happen on Game of Thrones especially now  that the HBO show has bypassed its  source material the eighth and final  season of Thrones is no exception to  this rule of unpredictability but the  most recent episode may have actually  spoiled the finale a melancholy song  lady Brienne Squire Podrick played by  Daniel Portman sings during a night of  the Seven Kingdoms seems to foreshadow  which person vying for the Iron Throne  will end up ruling warning spoilers  ahead The Musical moment happens while  Podrick Brienne Jaime Lannister tormund  Giantsbane Tyrion Lannister and sir  table OC worth are gathered around a  fire awaiting the arrival of the night  King and the army of the dead they drink  and reminisce on past battles on what  could be the last night of their lives  when the wine runs out  Tyrion requests someone sing a song no  one but Podrick pipes up and he begins  singing a mournful tune dance with her  go he continues with lyrics about how  Jenny couldn't remember the ghost names  but they took away her sorrow and pain  by spinning her on an old stone the song  then repeats that she never wanted to  leave this scene did more than just tug  on heartstrings as it played over shots  of our heroes in Winterfell readying  themselves for battle it evoked the mood  Pippin created when he sang the edge of  night ahead of the Battle of Askia in  The Lord of the Rings in the Song of Ice  and Fire books this tune is titled Jenny  song and is directly connected to the  series central characters and their  ancestors  Jenny song appears in the novel's is one  of the ghosts of high hearts favorite  songs which she refers to as my Jenny  song Jenny is Jenny of old stones a low  status woman who married Prince Duncan  Targaryen their union which Prince  Duncan's father King Aegon v disapproved  of spurred Prince Duncan to renounce his  claim to the Iron Throne despite being  the rightful heir in the same way Jaime  Lannister shoved bran stark out of a  Winterfell tower to protect his  incestuous relationship with his sister  Cersei Prince Duncan made the bold  decision to abdicate the throne to marry  Jenny not only does Jenny and Duncan's  story mirror that of Jaime and  it also parallels to other Targaryen Jon  Snow whose real name is Aegon Targaryen  and Daenerys in episode 2 John reveals  to his ladylove that he's actually her  nephew the son of her brother Rhaegar  Targaryen and Lyanna Stark that makes  him the rightful heir to the Iron Throne  given he's a living male descendant of  Aerys the Mad King Targaryen Podrick  singing jenny's song just before that  conversation happens might foreshadow  the events of the game of Thrones finale  John could relinquish his power to be  with Daenerys just as Prince Duncan did  it's doubtful that Podrick knew  everything about John's parentage and  the story of Jenny and Duncan when he  decided to sing the sad tune but there's  even more hidden meaning in the song  that supports the idea John may give up  the Iron Throne to be with Daenerys you  didn't tell me you were going to abandon  your crown I never wanted a crown the  ghost of high heart is thought to be the  first person who delivered the prophecy  that Eris and raela Targaryen Danny's  parents and John's grandparents could be  the ancestors of the prince that was  promised Rhaegar Danny's brother grew  obsessive over the prophecy believing he  was the prince that was promised he  thought that if he wasn't the prince one  of his children would be as vanity  fair-- notes Rhaegar may have actually  written Jenny song in the books during  the tourney of Harrenhal he plays a song  for his love  Fionna stark Jon Snow's mother it's not  out of the realm of possibility that the  tune was the one Podrick sang just after  Podrick sings Jenny song John and  Daenerys stand in front of lyanna  stark's statue in the Winterfell crypts  Daenerys says about Rhaegar everyone  told me he was decent and kind he'd like  to sing there's a chance that Jenny song  is more about the prince that was  promised prophecy than Jenny herself it  tells the story of the true born heir to  the Iron Throne giving up everything for  love  John Rhaegar son might be both the  prince that was promised and someone who  like his ancestor Duncan surrenders his  claim to kingship there really is no  telling whether Jenny song and its many  meanings reflect how the series will  conclude or whether Jon will actually  choose love over power but there's a  chance that the tune hints at what will  happen if it winds up that Jenny song is  more than a tune sung in an emotional  time at least Daniel Portman got to  prove he has the voice of an angel check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about Game  of Thrones are coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

